# Realm Labs CRM — rules for every prompt

You are building the Realm Labs CRM. Follow these rules without exception.

1. TypeScript strict mode everywhere. No `any`.
2. All API inputs and outputs are validated with Zod schemas from `packages/contracts`. Never inline a schema in a route.
3. Every DB table has `id` (uuid), `created_at`, `updated_at`. Soft delete via `deleted_at` where noted. `email_suppressions` is never soft-deleted.
4. All timestamps stored in UTC. Display in `America/Los_Angeles`.
5. Keyboard first UI. Every board and list is navigable with `j`/`k`, enter, esc. Minimal chrome.
6. No feature not in this spec. If something seems missing, add a TODO comment, do not invent scope.
7. Every mutation writes an activity row (who, what, when, before, after).
8. Do not write tests for UI. Do write tests for routing logic, report math, email matching, scoring math, suppression precedence, and unsubscribe GET-never-writes.
9. Operator mailboxes are `nathan@realmlabs.co` (`personal`) and `stefano@realmlabs.co` (`partner`). There is no `application@` shared inbox. Each operator connects Gmail readonly and Calendar readonly. Matched contact threads are visible to every operator. Unmatched threads are visible only to that mailbox owner unless `shared_visible` is true. Home tasks are visible to the operator who created them; admin can toggle all operators on Home. Contact-record tasks are visible to every operator. Admin can connect any mailbox; a member can connect only their own.
10. Suppression is HMAC-SHA256 of `canonicalEmail`, not person id. Write the tombstone before purge. Reasons: `unsubscribed`, `complained`, `hard_bounced`, `do_not_contact`, `rejected`, `enrolled`. Suppression always wins over score, program, tag, and consent. Never rotate `EMAIL_HASH_KEY`.
11. Consent is separate from suppression: `inquiry`, `newsletter`, `stay_in_touch`. Leaving the newsletter does not purge. Scores are 0–100 append-only snapshots; `lead_temp` is the derived campaign bucket.
12. Campaign mail is `@mail.realmlabs.co` only. Enqueue is not send: drain claims `queued → sending` before Postmark, then marks sent. GET `/api/unsubscribe/:token` is confirm-only; POST writes. Kickbox is new website form intake only. `POSTMARK_SEND_ENABLED` defaults off and requires `ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL`.
